  "decisionSummary": "The dev-publish v13/0.0.13 source is canonical. Jinn had THREE stacked defects and each fix exposed the next. v11 fixed the keybox first-save, which a fresh grain proved (keybox.json created, created=true, zero keybox errors \u2014 v10 never managed it). v12 then failed on the next line with 'sqlitestore: pragma \"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL\": unable to open database file: out of memory (14)'; I read that as RLIMIT_AS starvation and shipped requestedMemoryGiB, and the tenant DISPROVED it \u2014 identical failure with the declaration in place (C-067). The real cause was the keybox bug one package over: sqlitestore reached the database through /proc/self/fd in three places and a production grain has no /proc (F-268). Fixed in grain-crypto-journal e7c60d2, which resolves by plain path while keeping the TOCTOU defence, since every call site is already preceded by validateNamedPath().",
  "internalControls": {
    "status": "passed",
    "checks": [
      "clean tracked dev-publish source at the selected commit; make test green and make pack clean",
      "two INDEPENDENT fresh recursive clones at DIFFERENT paths produced identical packages: packageId f7804cbaa1837e8bc4cce215cfeb859f, sha256 f7804cbaa1837e8bc4cce215cfeb859f5e3e40cdbad70107706eed28876e9845",
      "reproducibility confirmed independently of the packer's own report: sha256sum matched and cmp reported identical bytes",
      "the keybox half is ALREADY PROVEN on the tenant at v11: keybox.json created, created=true, zero keybox errors",
      "the sqlitestore fix carries its own guard, TestStorePathIsNotProcIndirection, with a mutation control: restoring the /proc form fails it by name",
      "HONEST LIMIT: neither guard can reproduce the original failure, because a workstation always has /proc \u2014 which is exactly why both bugs survived local testing. Each pins the property that broke instead, and the decisive control is a live grain.",
      "KNOWN RESIDUAL (F-267, not fixed here): any failure between keybox creation and store creation still leaves that grain unable to initialise, because creation authority derives from having created the keybox in the same call",
      "STILL OWED: governed publication, then a clean-tenant fresh-grain runtime proof at v13."
    ]
  },
